          "severity": "Low",
          "criterion": "material_exceptions",
          "location": "orientation[2] and comparison_tables[0] (the numbers table); bears on practice_question_ids MA-Q-0245 choice E",
          "problem": "The section teaches 247 CMR 8.01(1), (4), (11), (12) and (13) but never states 247 CMR 8.01(5), 'Pharmacy internship hours may be acquired throughout a calendar year.' That one-line provision is the direct textual answer to the distractor in MA-Q-0245 choice E ('All 1500 hours must be acquired within a single calendar year').",
          "rationale": "No proposition in the section is wrong and none imposes a temporal limit, so a candidate working from the section will still reject choice E as unsupported; the out-of-state credit rule in 8.01(11) taught at exceptions[1] also cuts against any single-year reading. The gap is completeness within 8.01 rather than legal distortion, so it is weighed as Low and does not defeat publication.",
