      "practice_mapping_verdict": "PASS",
      "summary": "Every legal proposition in this section was checked against the current official text of 247 CMR 8.01 (4/25/25 edition, effective 1/9/25), the 247 CMR 2.00 definitions of Preceptor, Direct Supervision and Pharmacy Intern, 247 CMR 9.01(17), 247 CMR 8.08 and 247 CMR 3.05, and each one is accurate. The 1500/1000/500 composition and the separate 8.01(1)(b) experiential pathway, the 12-hour daily credit ceiling in 8.01(4) held apart from the 12-hours-in-24 practice limit and eight-consecutive-hour rest period in 9.01(17) with its extenuating-circumstance exception, the two-intern preceptor cap in 8.01(16), the intern's authority to supervise pharmacy technicians while itself directly supervised under 8.01(15), the three entry routes in 8.01(7), (8) and (10), the Board's credit determinations under 8.01(11) and (12), the 14-day withdrawal notice in 8.01(18), and the discretionary and additive examination bar in 8.01(17) are all stated faithfully, with the correct actor on each duty. The preceptor definition is read from 247 CMR 2.00 rather than from the operative paragraph alone, and direct supervision is correctly stated to include directly reviewing the intern's work. All ten listed practice questions (MA-Q-0077, 0078, 0229, 0230, 0242, 0243, 0244, 0245, 0273, 0276) are answerable from the section and none is contradicted by it. The single finding is a Low completeness gap: 247 CMR 8.01(5) is not taught."
