      "practice_mapping_verdict": "PASS",
      "summary": "Checked against the current official 247 CMR 8.02, 8.03, 8.04, 8.06, 8.07 and 8.08, the 247 CMR 2.00 definitions, 247 CMR 9.04(8), and the 12th Amendment to the PREP Act COVID-19 Declaration at 89 FR 99875, every proposition is accurate. The four common eligibility requirements and the three alternatives in 8.02(3), the prerequisite structure of the examination route in 8.02(3)(e)3, the four training-program categories in 8.02(4) with the separate 120-hour theoretical and 120-hour practical minimums, the 8.02(3)(e)3.a topic list, the six examination knowledge areas in 8.02(5), the two-year birthdate expiry and unlicensed-practice consequence in 8.07 with the over-two-year condition power, the 16-year floor and 1500-hour/one-year trainee cap with its three exceptions and the 30-day post-18th-birthday application, the trainee telephone carve-out written as an exception to the grant it qualifies, the closed prohibition lists in 8.02(6)(d) and 8.04(4)(e), the unchanged-information condition on 8.02(6)(c) and its deliberate absence from 8.04(4)(c), the Schedule VI-only transfer authority, and the three simultaneous consequences of a lapsed certification in 8.04(3) are all stated faithfully, with the correct tier and condition attached in each case. Federal verification confirmed the technician conditions (State licensure or registration, a readily and immediately available supervising pharmacist, an ACPE-approved practical training program, a current basic CPR certificate), the preemption statement, and the December 31, 2029 end date, and confirmed that no later amendment supersedes 89 FR 99875. All fourteen listed practice questions are answerable from the section and none is contradicted by it. The single finding is a Low presentational mismatch between two correct statements of the influenza age limb."
