          "criterion": "actor_and_scope",
          "location": "comparison_tables[0] ('Schedule II stock by personnel tier under 247 CMR 8.05'), rows[1] (Pharmacy intern), cells[1] and cells[2]",
          "problem": "In a tier-by-tier permission table the pharmacy intern row answers 'Not named in 247 CMR 8.05(2)' for both assisting in transporting and assisting in handling Schedule II controlled substances. That is textually exact about 8.05(2), but a reader scanning the table for what each tier may do could take it as a prohibition on interns.",
          "rationale": "247 CMR 2.00 defines a Pharmacy Intern as able to engage in the full range of activities conducted by a registered pharmacist provided the intern is at all times under the direct supervision of a registered pharmacist preceptor, and 247 CMR 8.01(3) states that supervision requirement, so an intern's authority over Schedule II stock does not depend on being named in 8.05(2). The section never asserts the contrary, states the point correctly in orientation[4] ('the one express permission the section gives a pharmacy intern is in 247 CMR 8.05(3)'), and affirmatively teaches at worked_examples[3], exceptions[1], quick_review[9] and role_duties[5] that an intern under direct supervision may handle the one product no technician grade may touch, which makes the wrong inference unlikely. Weighed as Low.",
