      "practice_mapping_verdict": "PASS",
      "summary": "Checked against the current official 247 CMR 8.01(14), 8.02(6)(a), 8.03(4)(a), 8.04(3)-(4)(a), 8.05, 8.06 and 247 CMR 9.23(5), together with the 247 CMR 2.00 definitions, every proposition is accurate. The counted population under 8.06(3)(a) is correctly tied to the four defined categories the pharmacist is utilizing to assist in filling prescriptions, and the 8.06(3)(b) exclusion is correctly stated as two limbs with the second conditioned on the person not supporting the pharmacist in any professional capacity, so that it can be lost mid-shift. The three alternative composition conditions for a four-person ratio and the single condition on a three-person ratio are quoted faithfully, and every roster worked through the comparison table resolves the way the text requires. The four name-tag provisions are correctly distinguished, including that only 247 CMR 8.01(14) asks for the intern's name rather than a first name, and the title is correctly tied to the credential held with the 8.04(3) lapse consequence applied. The Schedule II allocation is right: transporting to the pharmacy technician under 8.05(2)(a), transporting and handling to the certified pharmacy technician under 8.05(2)(b), the pharmacist's approval evidenced by written policies and procedures treated as a condition on each grant rather than as a source of authority, accountability and security left with the pharmacist under 8.05(1), and the 8.05(3) prohibition correctly drawn by product and formulation across all three technician grades with the express intern permission. The 8.06(1) duty is correctly characterised as production on request with pharmacy interns absent from all three items, and the 30-day, five-day and 100-day thresholds in 9.23(5) are placed on the right branches with the inventory duty reassigned rather than excused. All eight listed practice questions are answerable from the section and none is contradicted by it. The single finding is a Low presentational risk in the intern row of the Schedule II table."
